course: dictionary
lesson: 444
title: Architecture: buildings, style and plans
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Architecture is the art and work of designing buildings. It can also mean the style of buildings in a place or time. Read the clues around the word: «Architecture is the art of designing buildings: an architect draws the plans, engineers check the building will stand up, and a big team of builders actually makes it.» The architect, plans and builders show that architecture is about planning how a building is designed, before anyone builds it.
explain: Context helps with other meanings too. If you read about a cathedral with pointed arches and tall windows, and the text says «Gothic architecture», the word means the style of building from that time and place. Check it by swapping in your meaning: "the style of buildings in a time or place" still makes sense.
explain: The same word is used for computers. The architecture of a computer or program is the way its parts are planned and put together. The words computer, parts and put together are your clues. Here architecture does not mean a building at all, so always read the whole sentence before you decide.
fact: Architecture means the art and work of designing buildings.
fact: An architect is a person who designs buildings.
fact: Architecture can mean the style of buildings in a place or time, such as «Gothic» or «Roman architecture».
fact: For a computer or program, architecture means the way its parts are planned and put together.
fact: Architecture is uncountable, so you do not say «an architecture» or «architectures».
exercise: «Architecture is the art of designing buildings: an architect draws the plans, engineers check the building will stand up, and a big team of builders actually makes it.» What is architecture? | Selling houses to families | Painting pictures of houses | Cleaning old castles | *The art and work of designing buildings
exercise: Ella says «Gothic architecture» means a kind of pizza. What does architecture mean here? | *The style of buildings in a place or time | A team of builders | The name of a computer | A kind of drawing
exercise: «The architecture of a computer or program is the way its parts are planned and put together.» What does architecture mean for a computer? | Its games and apps | How fast it can be sold | Its colour and shape | *The way its parts are planned and put together
test: Which job designs buildings? | Electrician | *Architect | Gardener | Plumber
test: «Roman» and «Gothic» are both examples of what? | Computer games | *Styles of architecture | Foods | Sports
exam: In «The architecture of the program is clear», what does architecture mean? | *The way its parts are planned and put together | Its price | Its size | Its name
